Marsh and Alamer used lavaan version 0.6-17. Also, in a recent post in the lavaan Google group, a user claimed to use epsilon values of 0.50 (link to post: EFA rotation: lavaan support for oblimin gamma and geomin epsilon <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/XNmfzKNaDTM>).

Therefore, and considering the error message provided by lavaan when trying to use an epsilon value of 0.50, is it no longer possible to use epsilon values for geomin rotation greater than 0.01?

